WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.690
Look down at your phone.

00:00:01.690 --> 00:00:04.500
It feels like magic, but inside,

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:08.110
it is fundamentally just a handful of sand from the beach.

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:11.780
Sand is made of tiny quartz crystals called silicon.

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:16.000
Humans figured out that if you melt sand down

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.500
and carve billions of microscopic switches into it,

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:20.950
you can trap electricity inside.

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:23.480
When a switch is OFF, it means ZERO.

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:25.670
When it flips ON, it means ONE.

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:27.500
That is all a computer is:

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:30.960
a beach of sand with lightning flipping switches.

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:34.000
So how on earth did we teach sand to think?
